Learning objectives
By the end of the lab you can:

reproduce the OLS slope and intercept from centred sums;
explain how centring changes the intercept but not the slope;
calculate RSS, TSS, \(R^2\), residual variance, slope standard error, and a confidence interval;
diagnose nonlinearity, unequal variance, non-normality, and serial correlation;
compare interpolation and forecasting validation; and
separate descriptive, inferential, predictive, and causal claims.

Run cells in order. Every # YOUR TURN cell has a following # CHECK cell. Before leaving, restart the kernel and run all cells.

